Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.40,0:00:06.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Agent of God, you say? In that case, try passing judgment upon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.85,0:00:09.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For I am the Strong Arm Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.14,0:00:12.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alex Louis Armstrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.99,0:00:15.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Allow me to show you \Nthe artistic alchemy
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.68,0:00:21.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that has been passed down among \Nthe Armstrong family for generations!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.96,0:00:27.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Another shot!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.84,0:00:38.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The opposite of destruction is creation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.86,0:00:41.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The opposite of creation is destruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.55,0:00:43.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Destroy and create.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.10,0:00:46.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the law of the universe!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.42,0:00:52.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll deal with you after I kill Fullmetal and Crystal.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.18,0:01:03.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A combination of physical strength and alchemy, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.48,0:01:04.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This could be trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.46,0:01:07.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brown skin and red eyes...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.38,0:01:09.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.51,0:01:21.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The god of your people strictly forbids alchemy, does he not?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.21,0:01:27.14,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,The transmutation process of alchemy \Ncan be broadly divided into comprehension,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.14,0:01:29.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,decomposition, and reconstruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.94,0:01:34.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You stop your transmutation process at the second one, decomposition.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.81,0:01:37.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is still unmistakably alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.71,0:01:41.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I do only as this arm instructs me to.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.63,0:01:44.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if it is contrary to God's will!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.89,0:01:59.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.60,0:02:04.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.88,0:02:09.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.62,0:02:15.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.96,0:04:07.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, now what do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.43,0:04:11.03,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Whatever we do, I'd like to stay as far away as possible from that guy in the sunglasses.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.62,0:04:17.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.68,0:04:30.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, do you have a back door?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.29,0:04:38.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're not going back to the Eastern Command Center?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.10,0:04:40.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Since Brigadier General Grand showed up,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.18,0:04:44.90,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,it could mean that there are reasons keeping even the Colonel from protecting Doctor Marcoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.90,0:04:45.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.99,0:04:48.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To make matters worse, there are all those people from Central here now as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.53,0:04:51.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are other people \Nhere from Central?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.44,0:04:54.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer and his entourage.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.70,0:04:56.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To catch me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.36,0:04:58.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, that's not why.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.14,0:05:03.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, okay, here we go!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.58,0:05:06.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on! Hold on! \NHey, hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.35,0:05:08.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, I'm gonna get you!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.31,0:05:16.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've had enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.08,0:05:21.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't care if I do \Nget killed by that man.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.85,0:05:27.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He has the right to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.19,0:05:41.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel! We found him!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.07,0:05:46.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.05,0:05:47.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, Major! What happened?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.90,0:05:49.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.57,0:05:51.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was close...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.83,0:05:56.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is intense.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.57,0:05:58.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel, what about Brig. Gen. Grand?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.70,0:06:03.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he's alive after that, \Nthen the Iron Blood Alchemist
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.70,0:06:06.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,can come back to life after \Nbeing turned into hamburger.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.09,0:06:10.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But he was an expert in military hand-to-hand combat, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.73,0:06:20.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was Scar, without a doubt.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.16,0:06:23.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.10,0:06:26.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's an Ishbalan.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.33,0:06:28.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major, don't get up!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.74,0:06:32.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm terribly sorry I could not \Ncarry out your orders, Lt. Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.40,0:06:37.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I saw him... his skin... his eyes...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.55,0:06:40.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those are definitely the traits of the Ishbalan people.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.98,0:06:46.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see. So that's why he's going after State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.46,0:06:53.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he's of the Ishbalan people, \Nthen why do you have to be killed by him?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.65,0:06:57.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Ishbalans instigated \Na war of independence, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.45,0:07:03.03,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,There were a lot of them who died, \Nbut the military also suffered many casualties.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.07,0:07:10.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If everyone who ever lost in a war \Nswore revenge, there'd be no end to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.64,0:07:13.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was no war.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.03,0:07:15.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was a massacre.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.83,0:07:24.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The people of Ishbal were \Na tribe in the Eastern Region
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.30,0:07:27.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who believed in Ishbala \Nas the one and only creator.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.22,0:07:31.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They held religious values \Nthat were different from ours.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.59,0:07:34.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We think of the world's composition
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.47,0:07:37.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as something which can be mathematically determined
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.47,0:07:40.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and have high regard for the \Nequivalent exchange of alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.69,0:07:44.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But the Ishbalans thought of alchemy as the work of the devil,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.57,0:07:48.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,which perverts the world \Nthat was given to us by God.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.30,0:07:55.88,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,As a result, there were resistance movements that sprang up from time to time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.46,0:07:57.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then, thirteen years ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.37,0:08:02.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, what do you think you're doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.98,0:08:05.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...while an officer was \Nconducting an inspection,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.01,0:08:08.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he accidentally shot a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.17,0:08:15.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That incident lead to the outbreak of large-scale uprisings and riots.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.38,0:08:26.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Before long, the rebellion had spread throughout the whole Eastern Region
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.81,0:08:30.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and had become a war \Nthat lasted seven years.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.41,0:08:34.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, in the final days of fighting...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.20,0:08:41.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the higher-ups decided to employ State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.04,0:08:45.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.21,0:08:49.55,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Because of their doctrines, the Ishbalans have neither alchemy nor up-to-date weapons!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.55,0:08:53.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you hope to obtain by further antagonizing them?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.06,0:08:54.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have you brought them?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.85,0:08:58.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're still under research.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.18,0:09:00.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, there's no need to use them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.39,0:09:03.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As a matter of fact, \Nthe rebellion is steadily spreading.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.39,0:09:06.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's because you're trying to keep them down by force,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.14,0:09:08.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and so, more and more tribes are cooperating with the enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.73,0:09:14.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you saying that what \Nthe Führer is doing is wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.24,0:09:22.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We already have several thousand soldiers
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.36,0:09:26.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and several tens of thousands of civilians who have become casualties.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.50,0:09:28.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is war.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.18,0:09:32.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Crystal Alchemist, let me see them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.80,0:09:55.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}In order to hasten the end \Nof this war, as of tomorrow,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.18,0:09:59.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I'm authorizing the use of \Nalchemic augmentation agents!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.60,0:10:05.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}So, then what happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.58,0:10:07.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.57,0:10:08.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.27,0:10:12.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For every battlefield \Nthe State Alchemists were dispatched to,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.89,0:10:16.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it was all over in one night.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.00,0:10:58.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There he is!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.34,0:10:59.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Over here!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.07,0:11:22.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yow!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.46,0:11:25.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.73,0:11:26.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let me see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.61,0:11:34.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the battlefield, \NI came across this couple.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.96,0:11:36.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They were doctors,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.36,0:11:39.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and would treat people, regardless of \Nwhether they were friend or foe.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.96,0:11:41.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.29,0:11:48.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.11,0:11:52.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was incredible, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.88,0:11:57.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, they died.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.30,0:12:07.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Grand, what's going on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.37,0:12:11.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This place has become a contact point for Ishbalan refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.23,0:12:12.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The doctors were \Nin cahoots with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.56,0:12:16.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They just wanted to save as many lives as they could, that's all!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.81,0:12:20.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The lives they save \Nare killing my men.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.84,0:12:41.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.48,0:12:46.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were just following orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.59,0:12:48.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The sin is upon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.45,0:12:52.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As fellow doctors, they saved lives...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.16,0:12:53.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,whereas I...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.97,0:12:57.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.44,0:13:02.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would you keep quiet and let me run away?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.40,0:13:06.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so, I left with \Nthe Philosopher's Stones
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.82,0:13:10.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and all of the materials \Nrelating to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.97,0:13:13.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it was too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.04,0:13:15.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The people of Ishbal \Nhad been exterminated.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.66,0:13:18.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that there were only a handful of survivors.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.69,0:13:22.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so, that's no reason for you to be killed!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.62,0:13:26.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He has a legitimate reason \Nfor his revenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.50,0:13:29.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can there be any legitimacy to his revenge
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.08,0:13:30.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,when he drags people who aren't involved into it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.12,0:13:33.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What he's doing...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.33,0:13:37.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is wrapping his ugly lust for vengeance up inside a claim of being God's agent
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.14,0:13:38.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and acting like \Nit's all noble. That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.75,0:13:40.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.84,0:13:42.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, if you had been...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.95,0:13:45.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would do the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.69,0:13:47.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the Principle of \NEquivalent Exchange, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.78,0:13:49.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.16,0:13:51.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Taking revenge won't ever bring anything back!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.75,0:13:54.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All you'd need to do is live.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.00,0:13:57.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Live... Live, and find happiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.83,0:14:08.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.83,0:14:17.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.40,0:14:19.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,why don't you come \Nhide in our hometown?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.69,0:14:22.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It won't even take three days by train to get there. Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.65,0:14:25.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'll be a little hard on us going back, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.09,0:14:28.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a house there, where an Automail craftswoman named Rockbell lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.94,0:14:30.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure they'd let us...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.06,0:14:33.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rockbell...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.74,0:14:37.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't go there... Not me...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.77,0:14:40.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.61,0:14:47.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What foolishness!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.88,0:14:52.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You would rely upon weapons that have been enhanced by the curse of alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.22,0:14:52.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case...!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.38,0:15:04.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's far enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.74,0:15:05.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Mustang!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.88,0:15:07.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mustang?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.61,0:15:09.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.67,0:15:10.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Indeed I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.33,0:15:11.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.98,0:15:15.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am the Flame Alchemist, \NRoy Mustang.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.43,0:15:21.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yet another who deviates from the path of God?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.26,0:15:24.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You would still challenge me to battle, knowing that I am the Flame Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.90,0:15:25.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.07,0:15:30.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.78,0:15:37.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why'd you do that \Nall of a sudden?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.82,0:15:41.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're good for nothing on rainy days, so please stay back, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.62,0:15:44.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't make sparks \Nwhen it's this damp, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.40,0:15:48.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.36,0:15:54.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He sure is fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.73,0:15:55.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After him!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.85,0:15:58.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Breda, you wait for Fullmetal at the train station.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.31,0:16:00.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why would Ed be going to the train station?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.81,0:16:04.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's obvious that he's thinking about getting Marcoh out of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.22,0:16:12.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.94,0:16:14.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait up!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.23,0:16:17.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We aren't going to take your research from you by force.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.45,0:16:20.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No! I can't go!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.18,0:16:38.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This time, I know that you are just a hollow suit of armor!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.42,0:16:44.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.25,0:16:58.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By joining your hands together, you create a ring
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.05,0:17:00.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and then transmute with \Npower that circulates within.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.10,0:17:04.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Without this miserable right hand, you cannot transmute.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.45,0:17:07.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will have to destroy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.72,0:17:19.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.56,0:17:24.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, run! Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.23,0:17:25.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.64,0:17:32.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will give you a moment \Nto pray to God.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.20,0:17:36.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, \NI've stopped believing in God.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.76,0:17:42.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You said your older brother died in Ishbal, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.91,0:17:46.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was killed... \Nby a State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.88,0:17:49.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm an older brother too.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.67,0:17:52.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kill me. It'll be an equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.27,0:17:54.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about, Brother?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.90,0:17:58.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You said yourself that it wouldn't be an equivalent exchange, didn't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.01,0:18:00.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's not a State Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.16,0:18:03.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I should be enough alone, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.51,0:18:07.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I promise you, I will not go after your brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.13,0:18:12.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, you are wrong, Fullmetal Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.82,0:18:16.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is nothing that can be equivalently exchanged
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.06,0:18:19.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,for the despair over losing \Nyour brother and your people.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.54,0:18:23.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If not, then what is \Nyour vengeance for?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.29,0:18:31.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! What are you doing?! Get out of there!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.22,0:18:33.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get up and run!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.08,0:18:34.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get out of there!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.28,0:18:39.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.50,0:18:41.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.31,0:18:48.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.91,0:18:52.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You dumb bastard, \Nhaven't you run away?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.31,0:18:55.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I investigated some ancient records once in Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.99,0:18:59.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In them, I saw the design \Nyou have drawn on your right arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.16,0:19:03.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This may be a dud, but it is still a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.14,0:19:06.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And sure enough, your arm is...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.12,0:19:07.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop! Don't say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.80,0:19:09.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.29,0:19:12.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san, is this different from when you were using the Stone's power?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.62,0:19:49.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The sewers, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.16,0:19:51.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't go after him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.77,0:19:51.78,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,I'm not going to!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.78,0:19:53.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yo!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.00,0:19:54.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it over?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.14,0:19:55.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as you're here, \Nyou could at least help us out!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.90,0:19:57.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lay off!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.10,0:20:02.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't go dragging a normal person like me into you ridiculous folks' freak show!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.39,0:20:10.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Hawkeye, take crowd control. Don't let anyone come near.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.51,0:20:11.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.47,0:20:15.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.48,0:20:16.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.48,0:20:17.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,stupid brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.48,0:20:19.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What was that for?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.48,0:20:21.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why didn't you leave me \Nand run away?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.89,0:20:23.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then you would've been killed!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.97,0:20:26.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So you decide to go and die instead? You idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.40,0:20:29.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you call your \Nolder brother an idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.24,0:20:31.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll call you that \Nas often as I want!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.83,0:20:33.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Live on, live on, survive,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.88,0:20:36.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and research more alchemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.48,0:20:38.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so that one day, \Nwe'll get our bodies back.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.09,0:20:42.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dying... Dying by yourself...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.88,0:20:44.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is one thing that \NI absolutely will not allow!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.00,0:20:53.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look, now my arm has \Nbroken off, you moron!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.07,0:20:57.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're falling apart, aren't we?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.61,0:20:59.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We must look just terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.32,0:21:03.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we're alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.50,0:21:06.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh-huh, alive...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.82,0:21:10.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That suit of armor...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.88,0:21:13.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've never heard of \Na soul transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.94,0:21:16.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He must've risked his life to take on that transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.44,0:21:19.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why the bond between \Nthose two brothers is so strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.04,0:21:20.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.88,0:21:22.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the Führer's secretary.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.96,0:21:24.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer's secretary?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.94,0:21:29.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer says that we will be taking custody of Marcoh
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.00,0:21:31.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that he will not \Ncome to harm.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.84,0:21:33.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.52,0:21:33.93,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.64,0:21:35.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.98,0:21:38.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's like I told you, Edward-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.68,0:21:41.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I cannot go to your hometown.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.30,0:21:42.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.72,0:21:45.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The doctor couple who died on the battlefield...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.09,0:21:47.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Their names were Rockbell.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.71,0:22:03.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's be going.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.03,0:22:11.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.27,0:22:13.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just heard Mom's voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.25,0:22:18.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dummy, you just had a brush with death. Don't start having unstable dreams, now.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.46,0:23:40.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.13,0:23:42.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 16: "That Which Is Lost"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.10,0:23:45.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother's arm and leg...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.20,0:23:47.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My body...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.19,0:23:50.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In exchange for having lost them,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.24,0:23:52.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,have we obtained anything?
